10:01.960 --> 10:03.370
Rumors?

10:03.960 --> 10:07.010
Put simply, they're slander.

10:07.910 --> 10:09.800
What specifically do they say?

10:10.710 --> 10:12.220
I summarized them here.

10:15.350 --> 10:16.680
Incredible.

10:16.680 --> 10:18.490
It feels malicious.

10:18.890 --> 10:21.440
But the rumors are entirely baseless.

10:21.900 --> 10:24.560
They could easily be written 
off as the product of jealousy.

10:24.940 --> 10:29.490
They're spreading among the 
first-years too quickly for that.

10:30.120 --> 10:34.200
Which suggests someone's actively 
working to spread them?

10:34.790 --> 10:39.380
Kanzaki-kun and the others from Class B 
think the rumors originate with Class A.

10:40.140 --> 10:43.580
Sakayanagi or Katsuragi, then?

10:43.850 --> 10:47.250
It seems far too obvious for them.

10:48.120 --> 10:49.840
That's the part that concerns me.

10:50.050 --> 10:55.090
What if we assume there's 
some truth to the rumor?

10:55.340 --> 10:57.540
Even if the rest were completely made up,

10:57.540 --> 11:00.460
that would greatly add to their plausibility.

11:01.070 --> 11:03.490
Has Ichinose denied the rumors?

11:03.490 --> 11:06.180
No, not as of yet.

11:06.180 --> 11:07.850
We should wait and watch, then.

11:08.170 --> 11:10.860
Even more so if they came from Class A.

11:11.820 --> 11:14.610
We have no reason to intervene.

11:15.250 --> 11:17.990
There's a chance it could make 
Ichinose perceive us as enemies, too.

11:32.870 --> 11:35.840
What would my brother do?

11:43.980 --> 11:47.730
Sorry to call you over 
this late, Ichinose-san.

11:47.730 --> 11:49.570
Oh, no problem.

11:49.570 --> 11:52.110
You're doing it because 
you care about me, right?

11:52.640 --> 11:54.990
You, too, Ayanokoji-kun. Thank you.

11:55.210 --> 11:58.310
I'm just tagging along with Horikita, though.

11:59.170 --> 12:01.490
It's about the rumors, right?

12:01.490 --> 12:05.820
Yes. Do you have any idea 
who's spreading them?

12:06.620 --> 12:11.180
I can't say for certain, but I 
think it might be Sakayanagi-san.

12:11.560 --> 12:13.030
What makes you think that?

12:15.340 --> 12:19.890
She kind of... declared war on me.

12:22.390 --> 12:24.890
I guess that's not convincing 
on its own, huh?

12:25.130 --> 12:28.980
Class A has determined Class B 
a threat worthy of destroying,

12:28.980 --> 12:32.640
and is harming you by spreading 
baseless rumors about you.

12:34.330 --> 12:36.230
I'm not sure about that.

12:36.670 --> 12:41.740
I think it should be up to you 
whether you believe a rumor or not.

12:42.080 --> 12:47.120
I feel like the best way to fight 
Sakayanagi-san is to stay silent.

12:47.350 --> 12:52.880
That will prevent collateral 
damage to Class B and Class C.

12:53.570 --> 12:54.880
You're a strong person.

12:55.240 --> 12:59.880
You're thinking about not just yourself, 
but the others around you, as well.

12:59.880 --> 13:02.890
I don't think it's anything all that special.

13:03.290 --> 13:04.150
Then let's work togeth—

13:04.150 --> 13:06.850
Please don't get involved in this.

13:07.600 --> 13:12.150
There's no need for you guys to get 
on Sakayanagi-san's bad side, too.

13:12.670 --> 13:14.650
You're sure about this?

13:14.920 --> 13:16.400
Of course!

13:18.400 --> 13:21.010
Thanks so much for worrying about me.

13:21.010 --> 13:23.370
But I swear I'll be fine.

13:24.610 --> 13:26.150
Thanks for having me by today.

13:26.570 --> 13:27.400
Later!

13:33.210 --> 13:36.550
Like I said before, we shouldn't get involved.

13:37.560 --> 13:39.870
If Sakayanagi is the rumors' source,

13:39.870 --> 13:45.270
we would put our own class in 
the cross hairs by getting involved.

13:45.800 --> 13:50.810
But if she takes Ichinose-san down, 
she'll come after us next.

13:51.050 --> 13:54.040
At which time Class B 
will already be crushed.

13:54.040 --> 13:55.670
That's beneficial to us.

13:55.670 --> 13:58.650
You don't care what happens to Ichinose-san?

13:59.770 --> 14:01.360
You're a very cold person.

14:02.180 --> 14:05.570
Isn't that the stance you've always taken?

14:06.350 --> 14:09.380
We'll eventually have to fight 
and defeat her, regardless.

14:09.870 --> 14:12.420
We have a common enemy right now.

14:12.420 --> 14:15.580
We can take down Class A and 
then duke it out with Class B.

14:15.580 --> 14:17.340
Pure idealism.

14:18.700 --> 14:19.940
I'm going, too.

14:21.200 --> 14:22.130
See you later.

14:32.300 --> 14:33.850
You're still here?

14:35.470 --> 14:37.720
Could we talk a minute?

14:41.880 --> 14:43.600
I don't know quite what to say...

14:44.680 --> 14:46.620
I really am sorry.

14:46.620 --> 14:48.250
For what?

14:49.080 --> 14:54.370
It seems like those rumors have 
you really worried about me.

14:56.000 --> 15:00.500
I really don't want you 
guys to worry, though.

15:00.930 --> 15:04.230
Is that what you're telling 
the members of Class B, too?

15:04.680 --> 15:05.360
Yeah.

15:05.680 --> 15:11.010
That's the line I'm sticking 
to until the rumors go away.

15:12.960 --> 15:15.050
That's all I had to say, so...

15:15.670 --> 15:17.520
Thanks for listening.

15:17.940 --> 15:19.050
See you!

15:33.700 --> 15:35.210
Unregistered Number

15:37.340 --> 15:38.460
Who is this?

15:40.450 --> 15:42.620
<i>Talk, or I'm hanging up.</i>

15:43.710 --> 15:45.970
Ayanokoji Kiyotaka.

15:47.070 --> 15:48.090
Who are you?

15:52.290 --> 15:55.220
<i>They're making their move, then?</i>

15:59.980 --> 16:01.410
What is this?

16:01.410 --> 16:03.040
Who put this in there?

16:03.040 --> 16:04.450
What's going on here?

16:04.450 --> 16:05.960
Let me look at that!

16:08.490 --> 16:10.210
Something going on?

16:11.000 --> 16:12.620
Ayanokoji?

16:13.100 --> 16:16.550
A strange letter was placed 
into all of our mailboxes.

16:17.290 --> 16:18.180
This one.

16:21.100 --> 16:24.250
"Ichinose Honami is a criminal."

16:24.250 --> 16:27.080
The ridiculous rumors have spread this far.

16:27.710 --> 16:31.950
After a blatant act like this, 
the school will have to get involved.

16:31.950 --> 16:36.270
And I'm sure the culprit is aware of that.

16:36.480 --> 16:40.020
Y-You know who the culprit is?

16:40.020 --> 16:42.020
I can't be certain, but...

16:42.990 --> 16:45.670
Come on, you don't have to 
grin and bear it like this.

16:45.670 --> 16:47.460
Let's talk to the teachers.

16:48.100 --> 16:49.730
It's getting really ridiculous!

16:49.730 --> 16:52.570
Yeah. You're an innocent victim here.

16:52.870 --> 16:54.160
It's fine.

16:54.160 --> 16:57.270
This isn't enough to get to me.

16:57.270 --> 16:58.400
Don't say that!

16:58.400 --> 17:01.710
If you don't do something, 
the rumors will just keep spreading!

17:01.710 --> 17:04.280
Yeah, we need definitive action here.

17:04.280 --> 17:07.570
Sooner or later it's all going to go too far!

17:10.830 --> 17:13.140
Hey, can we talk?

17:14.770 --> 17:16.980
You're from Class A, right?

17:16.980 --> 17:18.500
Kamuro Masumi.

17:22.030 --> 17:23.860
Your room is extremely plain.

17:23.860 --> 17:28.610
That's the first thing you have to say 
after forcing your way into my room?

17:28.610 --> 17:30.360
Forcing my way?

17:30.360 --> 17:32.110
I believe I got your permission.

17:32.110 --> 17:34.870
So, what do you want?

17:34.870 --> 17:37.670
It's going to be a long story, 
so you should get me a drink.

17:39.570 --> 17:41.620
Coffee or tea?

17:41.620 --> 17:42.980
Do you have cocoa?

17:43.370 --> 17:44.130
Yes.

17:44.130 --> 17:45.550
I'll have that, then.

17:47.010 --> 17:52.010
<i>I offered two choices, 
and she came up with a third one.</i>

17:57.490 --> 17:59.020
You're not drinking?

17:59.230 --> 18:01.070
Are you wary of me?

18:01.530 --> 18:04.020
Why wouldn't I be?

18:04.260 --> 18:08.210
A girl I've never spoken to before—
one from Class A, at that—

18:08.210 --> 18:10.030
is in my room.

18:10.480 --> 18:13.400
You're not at all like 
your classmate, Yamauchi.

18:15.320 --> 18:18.540
What did you think of that 
letter about Ichinose?

18:18.540 --> 18:20.290
I didn't care.

18:20.290 --> 18:23.270
Even if you didn't, you probably 
thought about it, right?

18:23.870 --> 18:26.690
Whether Ichinose is a good 
person or a bad person?

18:27.520 --> 18:30.800
Being a criminal doesn't necessarily 
make you a bad person.

18:30.800 --> 18:34.090
Sakayanagi knows a secret about Ichinose.

18:34.600 --> 18:36.100
Really?

18:36.100 --> 18:41.440
Just so you know, Sakayanagi doesn't 
know I'm here talking to you about this.

18:42.390 --> 18:44.310
I'm sure she'd be angry if she knew.

18:44.890 --> 18:47.070
I'm afraid I don't believe you.

18:50.320 --> 18:54.820
That's why I'm going to tell 
you what Ichinose is hiding.

18:57.530 --> 19:04.710
But first, I need to tell you 
why Sakayanagi works me so hard.

19:07.550 --> 19:09.550
It was after the entrance ceremony.

19:18.840 --> 19:20.100
Wait a moment.

19:23.270 --> 19:27.350
You shoplifted, didn't you?

19:32.080 --> 19:33.610
So what if I did?

19:33.910 --> 19:36.490
Your technique was impressive.

19:36.490 --> 19:38.170
I'll return it.

19:38.170 --> 19:39.240
Here.

19:39.960 --> 19:42.490
You drink alcohol?

19:42.730 --> 19:45.500
I don't actually, no.

19:45.500 --> 19:51.870
So you did it purely for the thrill, then?

19:51.870 --> 19:54.630
Why don't you just turn me 
in to the school already?

19:56.560 --> 19:59.020
Why don't you let me dispose of this?

19:59.910 --> 20:02.900
If you won't call them, I will!

20:04.690 --> 20:08.060
I like you, Kamuro Masumi-san.

20:09.000 --> 20:12.520
I think I'll make you my first friend.

20:16.250 --> 20:19.030
I was a habitual shoplifter.

20:19.330 --> 20:20.280
"Was"?

20:20.590 --> 20:22.630
I don't have time for it now.

20:22.630 --> 20:25.290
Sakayanagi works me too hard for that.

20:25.500 --> 20:27.540
That's why you came to me?

20:27.540 --> 20:28.790
Yes.

20:29.570 --> 20:32.600
Ichinose's secret is the same as mine.

20:32.600 --> 20:35.690
She has a history of shoplifting?

20:35.690 --> 20:37.880
Despite what a queen bee she is.

20:39.040 --> 20:41.300
So you need to stop Sakayanagi.

20:41.300 --> 20:43.270
You can make it happen, right?

20:43.770 --> 20:45.560
Why me?

20:45.970 --> 20:49.290
I don't have anyone to confide in.

20:50.060 --> 20:54.610
And you're the person Sakayanagi 
is most worried about.

20:54.610 --> 20:56.700
I'm honored.

20:56.700 --> 20:58.820
But I can't trust you.

20:58.820 --> 20:59.820
Why not?

20:59.820 --> 21:06.330
I could imagine Sakayanagi choosing to 
sacrifice you to draw me into the fight.

21:07.800 --> 21:11.080
I'll prove it, then.

21:18.420 --> 21:19.240
See?

21:24.110 --> 21:26.220
It does seem genuine.

21:26.220 --> 21:27.900
Of course it is.

21:27.900 --> 21:31.880
And it's not something a 
student like me could buy.

21:33.480 --> 21:36.730
I suppose I have to believe you.

21:36.730 --> 21:38.520
I'm glad to hear it.

21:38.910 --> 21:40.240
Good luck to you.

21:40.240 --> 21:42.530
Take this with you.

21:43.250 --> 21:44.540
Hey!

21:49.620 --> 21:51.620
Horikita Manabu

21:53.050 --> 21:54.380
Yes?

21:54.830 --> 21:56.150
<i>Ayanokoji.</i>

21:57.000 --> 21:59.180
<i>I wanted to inform you of something.</i>

21:59.690 --> 22:02.260
What, is that real Valentine's chocolate?

22:00.620 --> 22:06.180
<i>Kushida Kikyo has made 
contact with Nagumo Miyabi.</i>

22:02.260 --> 22:03.540
No, just obligation!

22:08.680 --> 22:10.020
I see.
